/* this part is mainly control certain functionalities in the model; does not change files*/

/**
 * This variable controls the method used for calculating organ growth in the model. It defines which factors 
 * (temperature, water, carbon, and nitrogen) limit the growth rate of plant organs. The value of this variable 
 * determines the constraints applied during organ growth simulation.
 *
 * The available methods are:
 * <ul>
 *     <li><b>TempLimited</b>: Growth is limited only by temperature without considering water, carbon, or nitrogen limitations.</li>
 *     <li><b>TempWaterLimited</b>: Growth is limited by both temperature and water availability, but not by carbon or nitrogen.</li>
 *     <li><b>TempWaterCarbonLimited</b>: Growth is limited by temperature, water, and carbon availability, but not by nitrogen.</li>
 *     <li><b>TempWaterCarbonNitrogenLimited</b>: Growth is limited by temperature, water, carbon, and nitrogen availability.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * The variable allows flexibility in how organ growth is calculated, enabling the model to be adjusted based on the
 * constraints relevant for different simulation scenarios (e.g., varying environmental conditions or resource availability).
 * For keeping the parameters more stable, we do not provide the options for 
 * the combinations of TempCarbonLimited as this would require changing the Lmax value which consider the water potential limitations
 * @TODO nitrogen limitations are yet to be added
 * Default is TempWaterCarbonLimited
 */
global String organGrowthMethod = "TempLimited";

